{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q60198809","formula":"C₁₈H₂₄ClNO₃","hill":"C18H24ClNO3","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":18.0,"H":24.0,"N":1.0,"O":3.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"SN 35210"},"descriptions":{"en":"SN 35210 is an arylcyclohexylamine dissociative anesthetic drug. It was derived from ketamine with the intention of producing a shorter acting agent more suitable to be used as a stand-alone drug, whereas ketamine itself generally has to be used in combination with other drugs such as midazolam to minimise the occurrence of emergence reactions due to its hallucinogenic side effects. In common with other short-acting anaesthetic drugs such as remifentanil and remimazolam, SN 35210 has had the chemical structure modified to incorporate a methyl ester group which is rapidly metabolised to a carboxylic acid, producing an inactive compound and thus rapidly terminating the effects of the drug."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":71769517,"mass":337.8,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC(=O)CCCCNC1(CCCCC1=O)C2=CC=CC=C2Cl","inchikey":"QFFBIIVCZDWTKZ-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"methyl 5-[[1-(2-chlorophenyl)-2-oxocyclohexyl]amino]pentanoate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"71769517","atoms":47,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":7.142,"y":1.585,"z":1.512,"el":"C"},{"x":5.862,"y":1.733,"z":0.896,"el":"O"},{"x":5.093,"y":0.608,"z":0.94,"el":"C"},{"x":5.422,"y":-0.45,"z":1.458,"el":"O"},{"x":3.765,"y":0.881,"z":0.272,"el":"C"},{"x":2.94,"y":-0.396,"z":0.11,"el":"C"},{"x":1.641,"y":-0.189,"z":-0.674,"el":"C"},{"x":0.631,"y":0.697,"z":0.06,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.604,"y":0.83,"z":-0.704,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.822,"y":0.061,"z":-0.266,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.597,"y":-1.472,"z":-0.247,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.068,"y":-2.051,"z":1.058,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.949,"y":-1.622,"z":2.217,"